The modules below are ports of the correspondingly named pyclarity 0.9.0
modules. Their structure, variable naming, numerical constants and behaviour --
including behaviour the upstream authors documented as defective -- derive
directly from that source. No pyclarity source code is redistributed here.

    src/jax_haspi_hasqi/ear_model.py    <- clarity/evaluator/haspi/eb.py
    src/jax_haspi_hasqi/haspi.py        <- clarity/evaluator/haspi/haspi.py
    src/jax_haspi_hasqi/hasqi.py        <- clarity/evaluator/hasqi/hasqi.py
    src/jax_haspi_hasqi/modulation.py   <- clarity/evaluator/haspi/ebm.py
    src/jax_haspi_hasqi/neural_net.py   <- clarity/evaluator/haspi/ip.py
    src/jax_haspi_hasqi/nalr.py         <- clarity/enhancer/nalr.py
                                     clarity/evaluator/msbg/msbg_utils.py

The neural network weights in src/jax_haspi_hasqi/neural_net.py are the
published HASPI v2 ensemble weights, transcribed from the same source.

The underlying algorithms are due to James M. Kates and are described in:

    Kates JM, Arehart KH (2014) The Hearing-Aid Speech Perception Index
    (HASPI). Speech Communication 65:75-93.
    Kates JM, Arehart KH (2014) The Hearing-Aid Speech Quality Index
    (HASQI) Version 2. J Audio Eng Soc 62(3):99-117.
    Kates JM, Arehart KH (2021) The Hearing-Aid Speech Perception Index
    (HASPI) Version 2. Speech Communication 131:35-46.

src/jax_haspi_hasqi/nalr.py implements the NAL-R prescription formula, which
HASQI applies to the reference signal. The formula, its 0.31 slope factor and
its six frequency-dependent bias terms are published in:

    Byrne D, Dillon H (1986) The National Acoustic Laboratories' (NAL) new
    procedure for selecting the gain and frequency response of a hearing aid.
    Ear and Hearing 7(4):257-265.

Note for anyone auditing this repository: NAL-R is a published linear
prescription rule, reimplemented here from the MIT-licensed pyclarity source
cited above. It is distinct from NAL-NL1/NAL-NL2, which are separate
proprietary procedures distributed under licence by National Acoustic
Laboratories. No NAL-NL data or code is present here.

The reference values in src/jax_haspi_hasqi/_golden_data/ were generated by
executing pyclarity 0.9.0. They are measurements of that software's output,
not a copy of it. See tools/generate_goldens.py.
